    ('44428a81-cfc8-4e6b-9671-f40a385b2c4f'::uuid, 'card_description', 'One of the world''s best-preserved Roman theatres, the Roman Theatre of Philippopolis curves in a semi-circle 82 meters across in the heart of modern Plovdiv, built in the 1st century AD.', 'A superbly preserved 1st-century AD Roman theatre seating 7,000, built into the hillside of ancient Philippopolis. It still hosts live events.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:44428a81-cfc8-4e6b-9671-f40a385b2c4f:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''A superbly preserved 1st-century AD Roman theatre seating 7,000, built into the hillside of ancient Philippopolis. It still hosts live events.'' restored on Roman Theatre of Philippopolis', '58440b169830c0f6015e77f8394f8045f920a0e64a79ac50986dcab3667edb9e|a47fe4f25dd196362ec30552478b42989c8ef0a63215694319f791cc2cb15c1c|a47fe4f25dd196362ec30552478b42989c8ef0a63215694319f791cc2cb15c1c', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-009", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "One of the world''s best-preserved Roman theatres, the Roman Theatre of Philippopolis curves in a semi-circle 82 meters across in the heart of modern Plovdiv, built in the 1st century AD."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-009 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "it is one of the world''s best-preserved Roman theatres [S1]; it is called the Roman Theatre of Philippopolis [S1]; it curves in a semi-circle [S3]; it is 82 meters across [S3]; it lies in the heart of modern Plovdiv [S1]; it was built in the 1st century AD [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-025 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Roman Theatre of Philippopolis is a Roman theatre (central claim: what kind of place). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_theatre_of_Philippopolis]; It is one of the world''s best-preserved Roman theatres. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_theatre_of_Philippopolis]; It lies in the heart (city centre) of modern Plovdiv. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_theatre_of_Philippopolis]; Plovdiv is in Bulgaria. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_theatre_of_Philippopolis]; It was built in the 1st century AD. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_theatre_of_Philippopolis]; The theatre is a semi-circle in outline. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_theatre_of_Philippopolis]; The semi-circle is 82 meters across. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_theatre_of_Philippopolis]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4561c396-b590-47a8-b6da-c177870361bb'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Found beneath York Minster in the late 1960s, the Roman Column once formed part of the headquarters of Eboracum. Its eight drums of Magnesian Limestone rise approximately 9.5 metres.', 'A 1st-century AD Roman column that originally supported a great hall. It was built by Legion IX and reused by Legion VI three centuries later.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:4561c396-b590-47a8-b6da-c177870361bb:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''A 1st-century AD Roman column that originally supported a great hall. It was built by Legion IX and reused by Legion VI three centuries later.'' restored on Roman Column, York', 'ee22ea94682abd0388c9638d9446eae13a38cd56e519595c674137c7466d0d05|d8f0a63520b8f2b86848e2bf3b4f6dcc843723cf919690703a264139241ed2e6|d8f0a63520b8f2b86848e2bf3b4f6dcc843723cf919690703a264139241ed2e6', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-009", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Found beneath York Minster in the late 1960s, the Roman Column once formed part of the headquarters of Eboracum. Its eight drums of Magnesian Limestone rise approximately 9.5 metres."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-009 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "it is called the Roman Column [S1]; it was found beneath York Minster [S3]; it was found in the late 1960s [S3]; it once formed part of the headquarters of Eboracum [S2]; it consists of eight drums [S7]; the drums are Magnesian Limestone [S7]; it is approximately 9.5 metres high [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-026 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Roman Column is a surviving column of the Roman presence in York, England, just south of York Minster (central claim: a Roman column in York) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_column,_York]; The column once formed part of the headquarters (principia) of Eboracum, the Roman name for York [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_column,_York]; It was found beneath York Minster [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_column,_York]; It was found in the late 1960s [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_column,_York]; The column consists of eight drums [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_column,_York]; The drums are of Magnesian Limestone [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_column,_York]; The column is approximately 9.5 metres high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_column,_York]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('4695356b-52be-4152-8707-b1db00ef4707'::uuid, 'card_description', 'The Palaestra at Delphi, in the oldest existing gymnasium of the Greek world, has a court ringed by Ionic columns of blue limestone, with an undressing room and two rooms for ball play.', 'The Delphic gymnasium dates to the second half of the 4th century BC, the oldest surviving of its kind. Earthquakes and landslides have battered the palaestra more than any other part of the complex.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:4695356b-52be-4152-8707-b1db00ef4707:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''The Delphic gymnasium dates to the second half of the 4th century BC, the oldest surviving of its kind. Earthquakes and landslides have battered the palaestra more than any other part of the complex.'' restored on Palaestra at Delphi', '71a0580863310b3f5c078b30b82b42bb8e711fa3ae1caa6ab7f211aa225f21c3|c353b0d891fda95b738165c940666d6c06552a18c9296fe16f114201490f5d03|c353b0d891fda95b738165c940666d6c06552a18c9296fe16f114201490f5d03', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-009", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Palaestra at Delphi, in the oldest existing gymnasium of the Greek world, has a court ringed by Ionic columns of blue limestone, with an undressing room and two rooms for ball play."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-009 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is the Palaestra at Delphi [S1]; the palaestra is part of a gymnasium [S1]; that gymnasium is the oldest existing gymnasium of the Greek world [S2]; the palaestra has a court [S4]; the court is ringed by an Ionic peristyle (Ionic columns) [S4]; the peristyle is of blue limestone [S4]; among the rooms was an undressing room [S6]; among the rooms were two rooms for ball play [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-026 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Palaestra at Delphi is part of a gymnasium at the sanctuary of Delphi, Greece (central claim: a palaestra, the wrestling court of the Delphi gymnasium) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; That gymnasium is the oldest existing gymnasium of the Greek world [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; The palaestra has a central court [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; The court is ringed by columns (a peristyle) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; The columns around the court are Ionic [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; The columns around the court are of blue limestone [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; Among the rooms was an undressing room (apodyterion) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; Among the rooms were rooms for ball play (sphairisteria) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]; There were two such rooms for ball play [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palaestra_at_Delphi]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('480f44f7-ad94-4ea5-bad8-fde912fa692b'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Ekornavallen gathers Stone, Bronze and Iron Age monuments in one burial ground, among them the passage grave Girommen, a name that early writers say means the giant oven.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:480f44f7-ad94-4ea5-bad8-fde912fa692b:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description None restored on Ekornavallen', 'dc4c3ced7c887aca07b6470419748cf9ac4cf8189428ad344a8e8f5b56d15e01|9db755e3e259128ac838c2bdbd0397680aa425dc5985f6b5f7ce871c96ec0bba|9db755e3e259128ac838c2bdbd0397680aa425dc5985f6b5f7ce871c96ec0bba', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-009", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ekornavallen gathers Stone, Bronze and Iron Age monuments in one burial ground, among them the passage grave Girommen, a name that early writers say means the giant oven."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-009 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is called Ekornavallen [S1]; it is a burial ground [S1]; it gathers Stone Age, Bronze Age and Iron Age monuments [S2]; one of its monuments is the passage grave Girommen [S5]; early writers say the name Girommen means the giant oven [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-026 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Ekornavallen is an ancient burial ground (central claim), in Sweden [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ekornavallen]; It gathers monuments of the Stone, Bronze and Iron Ages in one burial ground [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ekornavallen]; It contains Stone Age (Neolithic) monuments [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ekornavallen]; It contains Bronze Age monuments [