    ('63c756cd-955c-4270-8474-916ed14fc2a4'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Along the processional ways of the Copán Ruins stood most of its portrait stelae, and Altar Q, dedicated in AD 776, has the first 16 kings of the Maya city''s dynasty carved around its side.', 'A Maya city renowned for its hieroglyphic stairway — the longest Maya text carved in stone. It ruled a vast kingdom in the southern Maya area.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:63c756cd-955c-4270-8474-916ed14fc2a4:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''A Maya city renowned for its hieroglyphic stairway — the longest Maya text carved in stone. It ruled a vast kingdom in the southern Maya area.'' restored on Copán Ruins', '2eed56c119275d99d1b6f58a724f130842ce998434e30a5c4681c1ba1b768df8|a262ae1c3ca31eb8a017fcc6c8e2eeb7a8cf050e5be92150333298eaa8dfd7d0|a262ae1c3ca31eb8a017fcc6c8e2eeb7a8cf050e5be92150333298eaa8dfd7d0', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-011", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Along the processional ways of the Copán Ruins stood most of its portrait stelae, and Altar Q, dedicated in AD 776, has the first 16 kings of the Maya city''s dynasty carved around its side."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-011 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "most of the portrait stelae stood along processional ways [S5]; Altar Q was dedicated in AD 776 [S7]; Altar Q has the first 16 kings of the Copán dynasty carved around its side [S7]; Copán is a Maya city [S1, S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-033 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Copán Ruins is an archaeological site of the Maya civilization (an ancient Maya city) in western Honduras [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cop%C3%A1n]; Most of Copán''s portrait stelae stood along its processional ways [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cop%C3%A1n]; Altar Q was dedicated in AD 776 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cop%C3%A1n]; Altar Q has the first 16 kings of Copán''s dynasty carved around its side [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cop%C3%A1n]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('63d56bb0-10de-42e3-ab43-c76ffca8c323'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Some 750 feet above sea level, Uley Bury''s double ramparts, more than a mile long, were terraced into the hillsides. Excavators found a crouched burial and iron currency bars.', 'A 13-hectare Iron Age hillfort occupied from 300 BC to 100 AD, with evidence of extensive settlement. It stands 230 meters above sea level with sweeping valley views.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:63d56bb0-10de-42e3-ab43-c76ffca8c323:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''A 13-hectare Iron Age hillfort occupied from 300 BC to 100 AD, with evidence of extensive settlement. It stands 230 meters above sea level with sweeping valley views.'' restored on Uley Bury', '2f54777678a23d705b1b0bd6ef178874358ef8585cb631d811cb4b804c70020e|dcf3d7e6e7dae927e5c241639679b6437862867722f295474c00b36b3ea7059b|dcf3d7e6e7dae927e5c241639679b6437862867722f295474c00b36b3ea7059b', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-011", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Some 750 feet above sea level, Uley Bury''s double ramparts, more than a mile long, were terraced into the hillsides. Excavators found a crouched burial and iron currency bars."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-011 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Uley Bury stands some 750 feet above sea level [S2]; it has double ramparts [S5]; the ramparts are more than a mile long [S5]; the ramparts were terraced into the hillsides [S5]; excavators found a crouched burial [S7]; excavators found iron currency bars [S7]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-033 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Uley Bury is a hill fort (an Iron Age hill fort) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uley_Bury]; Uley Bury stands some 750 feet above sea level [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uley_Bury]; It has double ramparts [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uley_Bury]; The ramparts are more than a mile long [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uley_Bury]; The ramparts were terraced into the hillsides [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uley_Bury]; Excavators found a crouched burial [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uley_Bury]; Excavators found iron currency bars [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uley_Bury]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('64f6ea93-b037-4a95-95e2-010e339fb0ac'::uuid, 'card_description', 'The sandstone capstone of Meehambee Dolmen, estimated at around 24 tonnes, slid back to a 45-degree tilt when its rear support collapsed. The portal tomb is dated to around 3500 BC.', 'A portal tomb from around 3500 BC with a capstone estimated at 24 tonnes. A supporting portal collapsed, leaving the massive stone tilting at a dramatic angle.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:64f6ea93-b037-4a95-95e2-010e339fb0ac:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''A portal tomb from around 3500 BC with a capstone estimated at 24 tonnes. A supporting portal collapsed, leaving the massive stone tilting at a dramatic angle.'' restored on Meehambee Dolmen', '57c18466c0f7799f61958fb36d9bf16bf7bf1448ab5e0cac44068d47bf157aa1|32bcaba86e8b21e4e6f4e576b382fca5a3df7854f2da662c4975a380ebaa8539|32bcaba86e8b21e4e6f4e576b382fca5a3df7854f2da662c4975a380ebaa8539', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-012", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The sandstone capstone of Meehambee Dolmen, estimated at around 24 tonnes, slid back to a 45-degree tilt when its rear support collapsed. The portal tomb is dated to around 3500 BC."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-012 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the capstone of Meehambee Dolmen is sandstone [S6]; the capstone is estimated at around 24 tonnes [S6]; the capstone slid back into a 45-degree tilt [S7]; the slide happened when the rear support collapsed [S7]; the monument is a portal tomb [S1, S4]; the portal tomb is dated to around 3500 BC [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-034 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Meehambee Dolmen is a portal tomb (a Neolithic megalithic tomb). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meehambee_Dolmen]; Meehambee Dolmen is in Ireland (County Roscommon, near Athlone). [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meehambee_Dolmen]; The capstone is of sandstone. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meehambee_Dolmen]; The capstone is estimated to weigh around 24 tonnes. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meehambee_Dolmen]; The rear support stone collapsed, causing the capstone to slide backwards. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meehambee_Dolmen]; The capstone now rests at a 45-degree tilt. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meehambee_Dolmen]; The portal tomb is dated to around 3500 BC. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meehambee_Dolmen]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('655898a6-3d5c-40f3-8411-e6b3b185f11f'::uuid, 'card_description', 'At Lerna, the House of the Tiles rose two stories under a roof of baked tiles; thousands of its terracotta tiles lay fallen in the debris. Fire finally destroyed it in the 22nd century BC.', 'A two-story Early Bronze Age building from 2500 BC with baked clay roof tiles -- among the earliest tiled roofs in the world. The tiles gave it its modern name.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:655898a6-3d5c-40f3-8411-e6b3b185f11f:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''A two-story Early Bronze Age building from 2500 BC with baked clay roof tiles -- among the earliest tiled roofs in the world. The tiles gave it its modern name.'' restored on House of the Tiles', 'c6341af283c33ef3eabc2f4a290653a181359802049a775741775a7f717c4341|a7ded7ff33d76235ba3fc601b42baa1dc67c7966bbd2e0f1adc680e4a414db1a|a7ded7ff33d76235ba3fc601b42baa1dc67c7966bbd2e0f1adc680e4a414db1a', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-012", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "At Lerna, the House of the Tiles rose two stories under a roof of baked tiles; thousands of its terracotta tiles lay fallen in the debris. Fire finally destroyed it in the 22nd century BC."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-012 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the House of the Tiles is at Lerna [S1]; the house rose two stories [S1]; it had a roof of baked tiles [S2, S5]; thousands of terracotta tiles lay fallen in the debris [S6]; fire finally destroyed it [S8]; the destruction was in the 22nd century BC [S8]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-034 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The House of the Tiles is a monumental Early Bronze Age building. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_the_Tiles]; The House of the Tiles is at Lerna in Greece. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_the_Tiles]; The building rose two stories. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_the_Tiles]; It had a roof of baked tiles. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_the_Tiles]; Thousands of its terracotta tiles lay fallen in the debris. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_the_Tiles]; Fire finally destroyed the building. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_the_Tiles]; The destruction by fire happened in the 22nd century BC. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_the_Tiles]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('658c8147-803d-4fa5-a335-bd1fe3573a28'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Sant''Agnello Maggiore, a church in Naples, was built above ancient Greek city walls of the 4th century BC, now visible in its transept, with 3rd century BC reinforcements in the nave.', 'Beneath this Naples church, excavations from 1979 revealed a 4th-century BC double curtain wall. The building was bombed in 1943 and left as a ruin until recent restoration reopened it.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:658c8147-803d-4fa5-a335-bd1fe3573a28:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''Beneath this Naples church, excavations from 1979 revealed a 4th-century BC double curtain wall. The building was bombed in 1943 and left as a ruin until recent restoration reopened it.'' restored on Sant''Agnello Maggiore', '68d2b987e7d4bf9f707859f770615f7dd9d0dac38341565ca29883d975522b50|03255fe8fdb2afce185e7a9b21a85d790452fec0e746144476b8b23290bce89f|03255fe8fdb2afce185e7a9b21a85d790452fec0e746144476b8b23290bce89f', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-012", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Sant''Agnello Maggiore, a church in Naples, was built above ancient Greek city walls of the 4th century BC, now visible in its transept, with 3rd century BC reinforcements in the nave."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-012 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Sant''Agnello Maggiore is a church [S1]; the church is in Naples [S1]; it was built above ancient Greek city walls [S2]; the walls date to the 4th century BC [S2]; the walls are now visible in the transept [S2]; 3rd century BC reinforcements to the walls are in the nave [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-034 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Sant''Agnello Maggiore is a church. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sant%27Agnello_Maggiore]; The church is in Naples, Italy. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sant%27Agnello_Maggiore]; The church was built above ancient Greek city walls. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sant%27Agnello_Maggiore]; The Greek city walls date to the 4th century BC. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sant%27Agnello_Maggiore]; The Greek walls are now visible in the transept of the church. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sant%27Agnello_Maggiore]; There are reinforcements of the walls dating to the 3rd century BC. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sant%27Agnello_Maggiore]; The 3rd century BC reinforcements are in the nave. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sant%27Agnello_Maggiore]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6726100a-71c5-44b2-9286-b176dd495a51'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Arsemia Ören Yeri was a royal seat of Commagene. Besides Nemrut Dağı and Karakuş, a third hierothesion lies here: the burial site and cultic area of Mithridates, father of Antiochus.', 'A 3rd-century AD summer capital of the Kingdom of Commagene, combining Greek and Persian architectural styles. A massive rock relief shows King Mithridates shaking hands with Heracles.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:6726100a-71c5-44b2-9286-b176dd495a51:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''A 3rd-century AD summer capital of the Kingdom of Commagene, combining Greek and Persian architectural styles. A massive rock relief shows King Mithridates shaking hands with Heracles.'' restored on Arsemia Ören Yeri', '846f65f8f1a8d4f33479fbb0f2cde580a43767799de2949f2046ef74b84f4219|882435d101aaf250bcadcfe3b15735cdc244cc58f91411a4511339bb80674484|882435d101aaf250bcadcfe3b15735cdc244cc58f91411a4511339bb80674484', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-012", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Arsemia Ören Yeri was a royal seat of Commagene. Besides Nemrut Dağı and Karakuş, a third hierothesion lies here: the burial site and cultic area of Mithridates, father of Antiochus."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-012 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site was a royal seat of Commagene [S3]; besides Nemrut Dağı and Karakuş there is a third hierothesion at this site [S5]; the third hierothesion is the burial site and cultic area of Mithridates [S5]; Mithridates was the father of Antiochus [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-034 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Arsameia (Arsemia), an ancient city at Old Kahta in Adiyaman Province, Turkey, was a royal seat of the kingdom of Commagene. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arsameia_on_the_Nymphaios]; Besides the hierothesion on Nemrut Dagi, there is one on Karakus. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arsameia_on_the_Nymphaios]; A third hierothesion is found at Arsameia. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arsameia_on_the_Nymphaios]; The hierothesion at Arsameia is the burial site and cultic area of Mithridates. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arsameia_on_the_Nymphaios]; Mithridates was the father of Antiochus. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arsameia_on_the_Nymphaios]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('6799d014-2963-4be7-954d-6a50ebbdcbc4'::uuid, 'card_description', 'The steep banks and ditches of Caesar''s Camp, an Iron Age hill fort south of Bracknell, trace an oak leaf. At its tip, multiple banks and a sinuous road guard the main entrance.', 'The hill fort covers an area of about 17.2 acres and is surrounded by a mile-long ditch.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:6799d014-2963-4be7-954d-6a50ebbdcbc4:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''The hill fort covers an area of about 17.2 acres and is surrounded by a mile-long ditch.'' restored on Caesar''s Camp, Bracknell Forest', 'a31f531b0ed1190f133703f31c04ddcb1daf3f2704fc7402897fa9917b6859ae|3377a6d6320b80575a3969673c34e69dfdc04605b57b959fa4e6861780664bbf|3377a6d6320b80575a3969673c34e69dfdc04605b57b959fa4e6861780664bbf', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-012", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The steep banks and ditches of Caesar''s Camp, an Iron Age hill fort south of Bracknell, trace an oak leaf. At its tip, multiple banks and a sinuous road guard the main entrance."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-012 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Caesar''s Camp is an Iron Age hill fort [S1]; it lies south of Bracknell [S2]; it has steep banks and ditches [S6]; the banks and ditches trace the shape of an oak leaf [S6]; the main entrance is at the tip of the leaf [S7]; multiple banks and a sinuous road guard the main entrance [S7]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-034 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Caesar''s Camp is an Iron Age hill fort. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar%27s_Camp,_Bracknell_Forest]; It is located south of Bracknell. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar%27s_Camp,_Bracknell_Forest]; The fort has steep banks and ditches. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar%27s_Camp,_Bracknell_Forest]; The banks and ditches trace the shape of an oak leaf. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar%27s_Camp,_Bracknell_Forest]; The main entrance is at the tip of the leaf. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar%27s_Camp,_Bracknell_Forest]; The main entrance is guarded by multiple banks. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar%27s_Camp,_Bracknell_Forest]; The main entrance is guarded by a sinuous entrance road. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesar%27s_Camp,_Bracknell_Forest]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('67b3a2f7-5f1b-46cc-893a-6cc48b2908c4'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Wapley Hill stands in mixed woodland on a west-facing escarpment: an Iron Age hill fort entered by a 90 m passage, and a late Bronze Age ''ritual shaft'' sunk to a depth of 33 m.', 'Wapley Hill is an Iron Age hill fort in Herefordshire 3 km south-east of Presteigne.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:67b3a2f7-5f1b-46cc-893a-6cc48b2908c4:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''Wapley Hill is an Iron Age hill fort in Herefordshire 3 km south-east of Presteigne.'' restored on Wapley Hill', '3b8d329f9d9d2acbaa8f58a0ec1ae4f75c9deb18e7bf55acb7a771957231fb21|027e7237e60cf05e63ba1551695e217c41dbe6d866a7f28a29f8d72c37946f81|027e7237e60cf05e63ba1551695e217c41dbe6d866a7f28a29f8d72c37946f81', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-012", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Wapley Hill stands in mixed woodland on a west-facing escarpment: an Iron Age hill fort entered by a 90 m passage, and a late Bronze Age ''ritual shaft'' sunk to a depth of 33 m."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-012 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Wapley Hill stands in mixed woodland [S2]; it stands on a west-facing escarpment [S2]; it is an Iron Age hill fort [S1]; it is entered by a 90 m passage [S4]; there is a ''ritual shaft'' dating from the late Bronze Age [S5]; the shaft is sunk to a depth of 33 m [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-035 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Wapley Hill is a hill fort (in Herefordshire, England) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wapley_Hill]; The hill fort is Iron Age [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wapley_Hill]; 