    ('7155aa5a-4eff-4b1d-a105-b15d17b786c6'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Quarry workers found Kirkdale Cave in 1821. Inside lay bones of hippopotamuses, elephants and cave lions, brought not by the Biblical flood but by hyenas that used it as a den.', 'Kirkdale Cave is a cave and fossil site located in Kirkdale near Kirkbymoorside in the Vale of Pickering, North Yorkshire.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:7155aa5a-4eff-4b1d-a105-b15d17b786c6:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''Kirkdale Cave is a cave and fossil site located in Kirkdale near Kirkbymoorside in the Vale of Pickering, North Yorkshire.'' restored on Kirkdale Cave', '7d7d11dd66111c32317c87cbbea7d0f55e8f27e509874e674bd3f04b72bb7aac|e146845a9a7539ecc13bc07d429ac2be2a757ffe17bf27a83a1bf8e031e0beeb|e146845a9a7539ecc13bc07d429ac2be2a757ffe17bf27a83a1bf8e031e0beeb', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-write-013", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Quarry workers found Kirkdale Cave in 1821. Inside lay bones of hippopotamuses, elephants and cave lions, brought not by the Biblical flood but by hyenas that used it as a den."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-013 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "quarry workers found the cave [S5]; it was found in 1821 [S5]; the cave held bones of hippopotamuses, elephants and cave lions [S3]; the bones were brought into the cave by hyenas [S2]; the hyenas used the cave as a den [S2]; the bones were not brought by the Biblical flood [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify-038 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Kirkdale Cave is a cave (in North Yorkshire, England) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]; Quarry workers found the cave [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]; The cave was found in 1821 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]; The cave held bones of hippopotamuses [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]; The cave held bones of elephants [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]; The cave held bones of cave lions [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]; The bones were not brought by the Biblical flood [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]; The bones were brought by hyenas [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]; Hyenas used the cave as a den [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkdale_Cave]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('71765908-34a8-4811-8e82-2e238a2bddfe'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Trogir''s historic heart sits on a small island between the Croatian mainland and Čiovo, 27 kilometres west of Split. Since 1997, UNESCO has listed it as a World Heritage Site.', 'In the 3rd century BC, Tragurion was founded as a colony by Ancient Greek colonists on the Illyrian coast from the island of Vis, and it developed into a major port until the Roman period.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:71765908-34a8-4811-8e82-2e238a2bddfe:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''In the 3rd century BC, Tragurion was founded as a colony by Ancient Greek colonists on the Illyrian coast from the island of Vis, and it developed into a major port until the Roman period.'' restored on Trogir', '86132edfa83c4d7c1c5278a78de4d9f63bb1bd25b102b02d13c4dacde646be51|2cc0a1624fe856b6b4887176da792798a4b943fa54cecebcfd66846145c2c178|2cc0a1624fe856b6b4887176da792798a4b943fa54cecebcfd66846145c2c178', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-rewrite-v-002", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Trogir''s historic heart sits on a small island between the Croatian mainland and Čiovo, 27 kilometres west of Split. Since 1997, UNESCO has listed it as a World Heritage Site."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-v-002 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the historic part of Trogir sits on a small island [S2]; the island lies between the Croatian mainland and Ciovo [S2]; Trogir lies 27 kilometres west of Split [S3]; UNESCO has listed the historic centre as a World Heritage Site [S4]; the listing dates from 1997 [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-verify2-005 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Trogir is a historic town and harbour (the kind of place) on the Adriatic coast in Croatia [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trogir]; Trogir''s historic heart sits on a small island [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trogir]; The island lies between the Croatian mainland and Čiovo [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trogir]; Trogir lies 27 kilometres west of Split [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trogir]; UNESCO lists Trogir as a World Heritage Site [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trogir]; The UNESCO listing dates from 1997 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trogir]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('71b04ac9-3273-4928-b38b-d830e7610755'::uuid, 'card_description', 'On Öland, Eketorp began as a circular stone fort about 57 metres across, thought to be a place of religious ceremonies and refuge; its full excavation yielded over 24,000 artifacts.', 'An Iron Age ringfort rebuilt across centuries — from defensive shelter to Medieval cavalry garrison. The only one of 19 Prehistoric forts on the island to be fully excavated.', 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:71b04ac9-3273-4928-b38b-d830e7610755:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description ''An Iron Age ringfort rebuilt across centuries — from defensive shelter to Medieval cavalry garrison. The only one of 19 Prehistoric forts on the island to be fully excavated.'' restored on Eketorp', '43c8b7622bff3b9c2e5619aa62a3a3cb1304793f9c8bff4a2df9169899970d85|5505dc5f3e507cf0092eeb59faaa397c819168216acef1ec4199409f27af349b|5505dc5f3e507cf0092eeb59faaa397c819168216acef1ec4199409f27af349b', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-rewrite-v-002", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On Öland, Eketorp began as a circular stone fort about 57 metres across, thought to be a place of religious ceremonies and refuge; its full excavation yielded over 24,000 artifacts."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-v-002 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Eketorp is on Oland [S1]; it began as a fort (original fortification) [S3, S5]; the original fort was circular and of stone [S5]; the original fort was about 57 metres across [S5]; it is thought to have been a place of religious ceremonies (hedge kept) [S4]; it is thought to have been a place of refuge (hedge kept) [S4]; the site has been fully excavated [S2]; the excavation yielded over 24,000 artifacts [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify2-006 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Eketorp is a fort (an Iron Age ringfort) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]; Eketorp is on the island of Öland, Sweden [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]; Eketorp began as a circular fort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]; The original Eketorp fort was built of stone [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]; The original circular fort was about 57 metres across [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]; The fort is thought to have been a place of religious ceremonies [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]; The fort is thought to have been a place of refuge [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]; Eketorp has been fully (completely) excavated [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]; The excavation yielded over 24,000 artifacts [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eketorp]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('72d00882-cac4-420f-8105-e1a0f7999340'::uuid, 'card_description', 'At Koumasa in southern Crete, Minoan tholos tombs were built of limestone without mortar. Outside one, a burial deposit held 140 multicolored beads and bands of gold foil.', NULL, 'teaser-card-s018-rollback:72d00882-cac4-420f-8105-e1a0f7999340:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s018: card_description None restored on Koumasa', '9b6e8deb1dde50d6caca7d6acb227053f26293e79f7e5f6a1c10089dbc9ff69e|14102790139182c935e971a6d59d188f6532f6f037f838bfb649d4a700040beb|14102790139182c935e971a6d59d188f6532f6f037f838bfb649d4a700040beb', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-rewrite-v-002", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "At Koumasa in southern Crete, Minoan tholos tombs were built of limestone without mortar. Outside one, a burial deposit held 140 multicolored beads and bands of gold foil."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-check-v-002 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Koumasa is in southern Crete [S1]; the tholos tombs are Minoan [S1, S6]; the site has tholos tombs [S6]; the tombs were built of limestone [S7]; they were built without mortar [S7]; outside one of the tombs (Tholos B) a burial deposit was found [S8]; the deposit held 140 multicolored beads [S8]; the deposit held bands of gold foil [S8]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-06: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-06-verify2-006 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-06/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Koumasa is an archaeological site (a Minoan settlement and cemetery) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koumasa]; Koumasa is in southern Crete [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koumasa]; Koumasa has tholos tombs [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koumasa]; The tholos tombs 